# Two rules, and no more. A .gitignore full of entries for toolchains this
# repository does not use costs a reader the time it takes to work out that
# node_modules/, __pycache__/ and build/ can never appear here -- there is no
# build step, no dependency tree and no compiler in this tree, only a Dockerfile
# and a workflow. Both lines below name something that can genuinely land in this
# working directory, and both would do damage if committed.

# Claude Code writes this file itself, to record the permissions a developer
# granted during a session on their own machine. It is per-person state that
# shadows the shared .claude/settings.json; committed, it silently widens what
# every later session is allowed to run without asking.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Anyone testing the image locally reaches for "docker run --env-file .env" the
# moment they want to pass an API key or a proxy setting to the container. No
# credential belongs in this repository -- the image is built with none, and the
# ones a container uses arrive at run time.
.env
